How to update service when printer is plugged in:

Preview what it will set:
python3 apply_pi_device_settings.py --dry-run
Apply changes:
python3 apply_pi_device_settings.py
Reload and restart service:
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart photobooth-preview-root.service


dependencies:

Go to your project folder
cd /home/bran/photobooth

Install required system packages
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y ffmpeg vlc python3-pip python3-pil python3-evdev usbutils libusb-1.0-0

Install Python print library
python3 -m pip install --upgrade pip
python3 -m pip install python-escpos

Give service user access to keyboard/printer device groups
sudo usermod -aG input,lp,plugdev bran

Reboot so group membership applies
sudo reboot

After reboot, go back to project folder
cd /home/bran/photobooth

Detect keyboard and printer candidates (optional report)
python3 pi_device_helper.py

Preview service updates without writing
python3 apply_pi_device_settings.py --dry-run

Apply detected service settings
python3 apply_pi_device_settings.py

Open service file and confirm these lines are set:

PRINT_BACKEND=escpos
KEYBOARD_EVENT_DEVICE=/dev/input/eventX
Either PRINT_DEVICE_FILE=/dev/usb/lp0 or PRINT_USB_VENDOR_ID and PRINT_USB_PRODUCT_ID
File: photobooth-preview-root.service
Reload and restart service
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart photobooth-preview-root.service

Watch logs
sudo journalctl -u photobooth-preview-root.service -n 120 --no-pager

Live tail while pressing space
sudo journalctl -u photobooth-preview-root.service -f

If printer is 80mm, apply 80mm settings then restart service
python3 apply_pi_device_settings.py --paper-width 80
sudo systemctl restart photobooth-preview-root.service

If USB-ID mode is needed instead of /dev/usb/lp0, run:
python3 apply_pi_device_settings.py --printer-mode usb
sudo systemctl restart photobooth-preview-root.service